ed is if we had  paid for our studio connect what is the  incremental cost of adding tableau  and i saw you had answered that there  oh i need to unmute you kelly sorry  there you go  okay cool  yeah so i answered that one in the chat  um we are not currently resellers of  tableau today in any capacity um that  that might be something we explore as we  do a partnership with them  potentially but today we have no  official relationship with tableau so  you have to  go through them to figure that out  unfortunately so i don't have any  information there  thanks kelly brody had asked could  something like plotley or hide chatter  be put into tableau via these apis  yeah so for that one i would explore  um probably iframing that application  that's been hosted somewhere else  or potentially that shiny tableau  package that  james previewed a little bit  a shiny tableau is a little bit  different than iframing because it  involves actually  building out a dashboard extension  and that's a little bit more complex but  the  documentation site for shiny tableau has  a little bit of a video that that joe  chang put together of  a demo of what that looked like so if  you're interested in learning more about  shiny tableau  i would start with the documentation  site and watching that preview video  thanks kelly  um i see that prabha asked are there any  enterprises known to the rstudio team  that have connected our studio connect  to an enterprise-wide tableau deployment  i know it might be a bit early for using  this  particularly but do you know kelly  yeah i don't think we have any examples  of customers who have  set all of that up and are willing to  talk about their implementation at this  point but  we can definitely  start thinking about that with our  product marketing team and i'm sure that  rachel would love to have somebody if  anybody on this call is interested in  setting something up once you are in a  good place to share what you've done  coming back to this gr